NEXA database migrations

Run `alembic upgrade head` from the backend directory before starting the API.
Docker Compose runs this command before starting Uvicorn.

The initial migration creates a new, empty database schema. An existing
database is adopted only when all current NEXA tables and expected columns
are present. Mismatched and partial schemas are rejected; back up the
database and write a reviewed migration for them. The initial migration is
intentionally irreversible to prevent accidental deletion of persistent
tables and records.
